(5737959, 832998, 98339, '<td valign="top">you know this to me is very underrated...the only drawback on this might be the lighting.  I scored this pretty high...</td>', 'you know this to me is very underrated...the only drawback on this might be the lighting.  I scored this pretty high...', '2009-11-23 11:07:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5738081, 832998, 61084, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ja-9:</b></div><hr/><i> you know this to me is very underrated...the only drawback on this might be the lighting.  I scored this pretty high... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks! I appreciate your vote Ja-9. I liked the way it looked and thought it would hold up a little better based on it''s symmetrical value (both the object and the overall photo) but after I submitted it and went back to it I realized I could have made it a bit better in PP which one simple step.<br/> <br/>I take it as a minor victory anyway because I have zero lighting equipment beyond normal tungsten and my camera flash which isn''t even a DSLR.<br/> <br/>Funny enough one of the things was most pleased about was the background. I hung one of my t-shirts on the wall with some tacks and shot against it. LOL. I think it came out good!<br/> <br/>Thanks again!</td>', 'Originally posted by Ja-9: you know this to me is very underrated...the only drawback on this might be the lighting.  I scored this pretty high...   Thanks! I appreciate your vote Ja-9. I liked the way it looked and thought it would hold up a little better based on it''s symmetrical value (both the object and the overall photo) but after I submitted it and went back to it I realized I could have made it a bit better in PP which one simple step. I take it as a minor victory anyway because I have zero lighting equipment beyond normal tungsten and my camera flash which isn''t even a DSLR. Funny enough one of the things was most pleased about was the background. I hung one of my t-shirts on the wall with some tacks and shot against it. LOL. I think it came out good! Thanks again!', '2009-11-23 12:10:42.000000', NULL, 0),
